  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian political landscape is currently addressing the departure of Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka. In response, the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has convened joint sessions to determine the legal and procedural path forward, including the creation of verification teams to manage the transition. While speculation regarding potential successors has emerged, various political stakeholders have publicly committed to maintaining government stability. Meanwhile, security authorities have adjusted standard protocols regarding the former vice president's protection in accordance with existing regulations. Economic observers and government officials maintain that the resignation should not negatively impact Indonesia's investment climate or economic growth targets, provided the succession process is conducted in an orderly fashion. The former vice president reportedly intends to remain in Jakarta following his exit from the executive branch, as the administration focuses on continuing its established governance and policy objectives.",
